<title>FRANCE: Basle-Mulhouse tops French regional airports for Jan-Apr.</title>
<headline>Basle-Mulhouse tops French regional airports for Jan-Apr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's top ten regional airports</p>
<p>for flown airfreight in January-April 1997, in tonnes with</p>
<p>percentage change on the same period last year, were:</p>
<p>  1.Basle-Mulhouse*   14,094   up     5.0</p>
<p>  2.Marseille	   13,886   down   5.0</p>
<p>  3.Toulouse	     8,413   up     1.0</p>
<p>  4.Lyon-Satolas	 7,827   up    11.1</p>
<p>  5.Lille**		8,555   up    13.0</p>
<p>  6.Nice***		5,674   up     2.3</p>
<p>  7.Bordeaux	     2,255   down  16.0</p>
<p>  8.Strasbourg	   1,666   down  28.3</p>
<p>  9.Montpellier	  1,631   up     3.2</p>
<p> 10.Rennes		 1,405   down  57.5</p>
<p>     *   includes traffic  handled in Swiss zone of airport</p>
<p>    **   also includes trucked air freight</p>
<p>***  provisional figures</p>
<p>The figures do not include France's major gateways for airfreight, Paris.CDG and Paris/Orly.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
